  "step_2": "The individual first considered Lottery A and noted the high potential loss of 6000€, which led to an initial inclination to exclude it. Then, they compared the losses: 6000€ vs 3000€, favoring B due to the smaller loss. Next, they compared the probabilities of winning 0€ (i.e., not losing), which are 99.9% for A and 99.8% for B, and noted that these are very similar. Finally, they revisited the loss amounts and their probabilities, concluding that since the probabilities of losing are nearly equal (0.1% vs 0.2%), the smaller loss in B makes it preferable. The justification is based on minimizing loss when probabilities of loss are similar. The individual focused on the magnitude of the loss and the near-equivalence of the probabilities of avoiding loss, leading to a choice based on loss aversion under similar risk levels.",
